  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that using 'transformer' aggregation and 'weighted' fusion with 'scvi_n200' RNA and 'imagenet_vit_l' image encoder achieves the highest accuracy (0.724989). This experiment tests whether changing the image encoder to 'resnet50' (a simpler, less complex model) while keeping other parameters the same affects performance. It isolates the impact of the image encoder choice, which is critical for understanding whether more complex models are necessary, and balances exploitation of current high-performing components with exploration of alternatives."
